# Agent Communication

**Canonical rule**: `../../.claude/rules/agent-communication.md` — read it before coordinating work across tickets or personas.

## Triggers — adopt this rule when

- Working on a ticket that has sub-issues or a parent issue.
- Handing off between personas (planner → builder, builder → tester, tester → shipper).
- Writing a PR description that other agents will read to continue work.
- A task spans multiple repos (cross-repo batch pattern).

## Key principles

- State is carried on the **ticket** and in **PR / MR descriptions**, not in chat history.
- Parent tickets summarize; sub-issues carry execution detail.
- Every persona handoff writes a short status note on the ticket so the next persona can pick up cleanly.
- When a ticket touches N repos with the same logical change, use the cross-repo batch pattern (one ticket, one update covering all repos).
